# Everything above the "Package:" line below is dropped by build-deb.sh, which
# builds DEBIAN/control by hand (no dpkg-buildpackage here), so this note is a
# safe place for it:
#
#   !! EDITING THE END OF THIS FILE: READ THIS FIRST !!
#
#   build-deb.sh's offline rewrite (OFFLINE_PAYLOAD set) drops every line
#   from " Building the UI needs" to END OF FILE and appends its own closing
#   Description paragraph. Two rules follow, and build-deb.sh enforces both
#   -- neither fails silently, but neither is obvious from reading this file
#   alone:
#
#     1. That marker line's exact wording is grepped for. Reword it and the
#        offline build aborts (rather than shipping a description claiming
#        the package is Architecture: all and wants Node.js from NodeSource).
#
#     2. Everything below the marker must be Description continuation prose
#        -- a leading space, including the " ." separators. A control FIELD
#        or a new stanza put down there would be deleted from the offline
#        package, so build-deb.sh refuses to build instead.
#
#   Practical upshot: ONLINE-ONLY prose goes AT THE END, below the marker.
#   Anything that is true of both builds -- fields, and prose -- goes ABOVE
#   it. Prose above the marker is shipped verbatim in the offline package,
#   so it must not describe how the online build works.
Source: c4raven-server
Maintainer: C4 Raven <support@c4raven.net>
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: c4raven-server
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: debconf (>= 0.5),
 curl,
 git,
 openssl,
 python3,
 python3-pip,
 python3-venv,
 python3-dev,
 python3-yaml,
 build-essential,
 postgresql,
 postgresql-postgis,
 libpq5,
 rabbitmq-server,
 nginx,
 libnginx-mod-stream,
 certbot,
 python3-certbot-nginx,
 ffmpeg,
 nodejs (>= 20.19),
 rsync
Description: C4 Raven TAK server -- full stack, single package
 A security-hardened fork of the upstream project this is derived from.
 This package installs the whole server: the Raven backend, the C4 Raven UI
 frontend served from nginx's webroot, a dedicated certificate authority,
 mediamtx for video streaming, and the systemd units that tie it all
 together.
 .
 Postgres, RabbitMQ, and nginx are pulled in as real package
 dependencies; everything specific to this app (the venv, the CA, the
 first admin account) is set up by this package's postinst script,
 which mirrors the previous curl|bash installer step for step. That
 includes opening the web, media and EUD ports if a firewall is already
 running; set RAVEN_OPEN_FIREWALL=false to skip it. No firewall that is
 switched off is ever switched on.
 .
 Building the UI needs Node.js 20.19 or newer. Ubuntu 24.04's own nodejs
 package is 18.x and does not satisfy that; 25.10 and 26.04 ship 20.19 or
 newer and do. On 24.04, install Node 22 from NodeSource
 (https://deb.nodesource.com, setup_22.x -- it publishes both amd64 and
 arm64) before this package.
 .
 The package is Architecture: all and builds everything on the target, so
 it installs on arm64 as well as amd64; every dependency above exists on
 both in Ubuntu. The offline build is a different story -- it carries
 prebuilt binaries, so it is built once per architecture.
 .
 The backend is cloned from GitHub and built with Poetry on first install,
 and the UI is built with Yarn on the target; both are pinned to the exact
 commits this package version was built against.
